(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "2607242700"), (:adr/title "kotoba-lang/stripe-ops -- governed Stripe Agent Toolkit-shaped actor for cloud-itonami flagship, read-only + Payment Link creation only"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607161745-cloud-itonami-flagship-managed-tier-stripe-billing.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607141700-cloud-itonami-git-native-business-cdci.edn")), (:adr/scope "new repo orgs/kotoba-lang/stripe-ops (langgraph-clj StateGraph actor, mirrors koyomi/shoko's governor/operation/phase/store/port shape) + a thin integration layer inside orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami wiring it as a tool into the existing cloud-itonami.agent ReAct CLI (:interrupt-before #{:tools}). Targets the 3 flagship verticals' live Stripe Managed Starter tier objects established by ADR-2607161745 (cloud-itonami-isic-6399/6310/7810)"), (:adr/why-a-new-actor-not-the-npm-stripe-agent-toolkit "Stripe's official `@stripe/agent-toolkit` npm package is the origin of this actor's tool-schema shape (customer/subscription/product/price read tools + payment-link create tool), but this codebase's Cloudflare Pages Functions `:edge-api` build target is deliberately zero-npm-dependency (cloud_itonami.edge.billing's own docstring: 'Talks to Stripe's REST API directly via fetch... rather than the Stripe Node SDK, matching this codebase's existing zero-dependency edge/* convention') and no evidence anywhere in this codebase of a genuine npm package being require'd into .cljc/.cljs that compiles under :edge-api (only Node builtins, and only in JVM/Node CLI-target files, never edge/*). So: adopt the toolkit's TOOL-SCHEMA SHAPE by hand in .cljc (tool name/description/param-schema + the same read+payment-link-create permission-scoping idea the real npm package exposes via its own `configuration.actions` allowlist), never add the literal npm dependency"), (:adr/scope-restriction-read-plus-payment-link-create-only "owner-selected scope (AskUserQuestion, this session): read-only Stripe lookups (customer/subscription/product/price) PLUS creating NEW Payment Links against an EXISTING, already-known Price id ONLY. No refunds, no subscription mutation, no customer writes, no product/price writes -- these operation kinds have NO code path in this actor's StateGraph at all (fail-closed unrecognized-op, mirroring koyomi.governor/tosmonitor.governor's own unconditional hard-hold on any :op the governor doesn't recognize), not merely a governor rule that could in principle be relaxed later"), (:adr/defense-in-depth-restricted-api-key-recommended "recommend (but do NOT create myself -- see below) a Stripe Dashboard-created RESTRICTED API key scoped to Customers/Subscriptions/Products/Prices READ + Payment Links WRITE only, as a SEPARATE secret (STRIPE_OPS_RESTRICTED_KEY) from the existing fuller-permission STRIPE_SECRET_KEY that cloud_itonami.edge.billing already uses for checkout-session creation -- so even a bug in this actor's governor logic cannot physically reach a refund/subscription-mutation/product-price-write call, because the credential itself cannot perform those calls. This mirrors the actor family's existing least-privilege credential-injection convention (shoko's r2-archiveport / koyomi's slack-scheduleport: credentials always constructor-injected, never env-guessed inside the library, real transport strictly opt-in over a mock default)"), (:adr/actor-shape "kotoba-lang/stripe-ops: model.cljc (known-price + payment-link-record shapes) / store.cljc (Store protocol: MemStore default + DatomicStore via langchain.db, known-prices catalog seeded with DEMO placeholder price ids -- never the real ADR-2607161745 1Password-held ids baked into this portable library -- + payment-links registry + append-only ledger) / stripeport.cljc (StripePort protocol -- the ONE place a real Stripe HTTP call leaves the building; mock-stripeport default with canned deterministic responses; live-stripeport takes a constructor-injected :api-key + :http-fn, JVM default is real sync java.net.http mirroring koyomi.scheduleport/slack-jvm-http-fn, no default on :cljs -- the caller must inject one, e.g. cloud-itonami.agent's existing node-http curl-based sync :http-fn) / advisor.cljc (mock-advisor default, mechanical pass-through + store-grounded confidence; llm-advisor swappable seam, unused by default) / governor.cljc (independent censor; HARD: unrecognized-op, unrecognized-lookup-kind, missing-known-price for payment-link-create, missing-idempotency-key, custom-amount-attempted (structural: only a known price-id + implicit quantity 1 is ever accepted, never an inline unit_amount/price_data override), quantity-not-one; :stripe/payment-link-create is ALWAYS high-stakes -> human sign-off, permanently excluded from every phase's :auto set, exactly like koyomi's :event/share / tosmonitor's :tos/change-proposal) / phase.cljc (0..3 staged rollout gating only :stripe/lookup's autonomy; default-phase 1 (assisted, most conservative), matching the repo-wide fixed-bug convention that an omitted :phase must never grant maximum autonomy) / operation.cljc (langgraph-clj StateGraph: intake -> advise -> govern -> decide -> commit|hold|approval, :interrupt-before #{:request-approval}) / sim.cljc + governor_contract_test.clj + store_contract_test.clj + stripeport_test.clj (fake injected :http-fn only, zero live network calls anywhere in the repo's automated suite, mirroring koyomi.scheduleport-test's Slack request-building tests)"), (:adr/integration-cloud-itonami "a thin projection layer (mirrors cloud_itonami.workspace's existing koyomi/shoko wiring: effect->stripe-ops-request translator + run-stripe-ops-lookup!/run-stripe-ops-payment-link! driving the real langgraph-clj actor) plus registration as a new tool inside the existing cloud-itonami.agent ReAct CLI (agent/cli.cljs), which already pauses at :interrupt-before #{:tools} for a human-typed approval before ANY tool executes -- so a human operator handling an ADR-2607161745 Next-Steps-#1 operator-interest issue gets a DOUBLE gate (this actor's own algorithmic Governor, independent of and upstream of, the CLI's separate human-approval-in-the-loop pause), not a replacement for either"), (:adr/credential-provisioning-not-done-by-agent "the actual Stripe Dashboard restricted-API-key creation (a credential-provisioning form) was deliberately NOT performed by the agent in this session (repo-wide safety floor: never fill in a credential form directly) -- this ADR documents the exact permission set + new secret name (STRIPE_OPS_RESTRICTED_KEY) for the owner to create and wire in via the same 1Password/Cloudflare-secret path ADR-2607161745 already established for STRIPE_SECRET_KEY; until that key exists, the actor runs only against mock-stripeport (safe, offline, no live Stripe account access of any kind)"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242700: kotoba-lang/stripe-ops -- governed Stripe ops actor for cloud-itonami flagship\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607161745 (the 3 flagship verticals' live Stripe Managed Starter tier\n  Payment Links this actor targets), ADR-2607141700 (git-native business CD/CI --\n  ops_governor.cljc's supported-kinds dispatch was considered and rejected as the\n  integration seam, see Alternatives)\n\n## Context\n\nOwner asked to set up 'Stripe agent'; clarified via AskUserQuestion (three rounds) to\nmean: introduce Stripe's official Agent Toolkit CONCEPT (LLM/agent function-calling\nover Stripe's API) for the cloud-itonami flagship vertical (extending ADR-2607161745's\nStripe billing work), scoped to READ-ONLY lookups plus Payment Link creation only (no\nrefunds, no subscription mutation, no other writes), implemented as a new dedicated\nkotoba-lang actor library (matching the koyomi/shoko precedent already established in\nthis workspace), integrated as a tool into the existing cloud-itonami ReAct CLI.\n\nResearch (Explore agent, read-only) into this exact repo's existing actor-wiring\nconvention found: every prior actor (teian/koyomi/kyoninka/goyoukiki/shoko/ichiran/\nkaisha/denrei) is a SEPARATE kotoba-lang library with its own governor/operation/\nphase/store/port namespaces, wired into cloud_itonami.workspace only via a thin\ntranslation layer -- never reimplemented inside cloud-itonami's own namespaces. It\nalso found that cloud_itonami.edge.billing's Stripe-calling code is deliberately\nzero-npm-dependency (raw fetch, hand-rolled form-encoding, matching the edge/*\nconvention), with no precedent anywhere in the codebase for requiring a genuine npm\npackage (like the real `@stripe/agent-toolkit`) into anything that compiles under the\nCloudflare `:edge-api` :esm target.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **New repo `kotoba-lang/stripe-ops`**, matching koyomi/shoko's exact shape (see\n   `:adr/actor-shape` above for the full namespace list). This keeps the new actor\n   directly comparable/reusable with the rest of the actor family, rather than a\n   one-off extension of cloud-itonami's own ops_governor.cljc (considered, see\n   Alternatives).\n2. **Tool-schema-only adoption of the Stripe Agent Toolkit.** The real npm package is\n   NOT added as a dependency anywhere; its publicly documented tool shapes (read\n   customer/subscription/product/price, create payment_link, each individually\n   permission-gateable) are reimplemented by hand in `.cljc`, consistent with this\n   codebase's existing zero-dependency edge/* convention.\n3. **Scope is structural, not just a governor rule.** The StateGraph has no operation\n   code path for refunds, subscription mutation, customer writes, or product/price\n   writes at all -- adding those later would require a new `:op`, a new governor\n   branch, and a new commit-effects! branch, not flipping a flag. `:stripe/payment-\n   link-create` only ever accepts a known price-id (from a store-seeded whitelist) +\n   an idempotency key; a custom amount/quantity-other-than-1 is a HARD violation.\n4. **`:stripe/payment-link-create` is always high-stakes -- never auto, any phase.**\n   Same charter as koyomi's :event/share / tosmonitor's :tos/change-proposal: a\n   human must sign off on every actual Stripe write, regardless of rollout phase.\n5. **Defense-in-depth: recommend (do not create) a restricted Stripe API key.** A\n   NEW Dashboard-created restricted key (Customers/Subscriptions/Products/Prices\n   READ + Payment Links WRITE only), separate from the existing STRIPE_SECRET_KEY,\n   so the credential itself -- not just this actor's governor logic -- cannot reach\n   a refund/mutation call. The owner must create this (credential-form safety\n   floor); this actor runs against mock-stripeport only until it exists.\n6. **Integration: a tool inside the existing `cloud-itonami.agent` ReAct CLI**, which\n   already pauses at `:interrupt-before #{:tools}` for human approval before any\n   tool executes -- giving this actor's own algorithmic Governor AND that human\n   pause as two independent gates, not a replacement for either. A thin\n   `cloud_itonami.workspace`-style projection layer wires the two together, the same\n   shape koyomi/shoko already use.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Extend cloud-itonami's own `ops_governor.cljc`** (its `ai-datacenter-handlers/\n  supported-kinds` dispatch is a real, precedented extension seam) instead of a new\n  repo. Rejected (owner's explicit choice) in favor of the separate-library pattern\n  for consistency with every other actor in this family and better standalone\n  testability/reuse.\n- **New Cloudflare Pages Functions HTTP endpoint** (`functions/api/.../stripe-ops`,\n  mirroring `billing_endpoints.cljc`) instead of / in addition to the ReAct CLI tool.\n  Not selected this round (owner's explicit choice was the ReAct CLI only) --\n  left as a documented future option, not built.\n- **Add `@stripe/agent-toolkit` as a literal npm dependency.** Rejected: no\n  precedent for npm deps under this codebase's `:edge-api` build target, and the\n  ReAct CLI's own real-time transport (`agent/node_http.cljs`, a synchronous curl-\n  based `:http-fn`) already gives this actor's `live-stripeport` a working,\n  precedented sync HTTP injection point without it.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) A new operator-facing capability for ADR-2607161745's Next-Steps-#1\n  (operator-interest issue -> present the right vertical's Payment Link) that adds a\n  second, independent (algorithmic) safety gate on top of the existing human-\n  approval-in-the-loop ReAct CLI, rather than relying on human diligence alone.\n- (+) Zero change to `cloud_itonami.edge.billing`'s existing checkout/webhook code\n  or its live Stripe objects -- this actor only reads and creates NEW Payment Links\n  referencing already-established prices, mirroring ADR-2607161745's own\n  no-code-changes-to-existing-billing-path discipline.\n- (-) Until the owner creates the restricted API key, this capability is mock-only\n  (no live Stripe account access) -- intentional, not a bug: credential provisioning\n  is a human, form-filling action this session does not perform.\n- (-) `@stripe/agent-toolkit` upstream schema changes are not automatically\n  reflected here (hand-maintained mirror, not a live dependency) -- an accepted\n  tradeoff for staying inside this codebase's zero-dependency edge convention.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607161745, ADR-2607141700\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/koyomi` (structural template), `orgs/kotoba-lang/shoko`\n  (credential-injection precedent), `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`'s `src/cloud_itonami/\n  edge/billing.cljc`, `src/cloud_itonami/agent/*`, `src/cloud_itonami/ops_governor.cljc`\n\n\n## 改訂履歴\n\n（2026-07-25 に `90-docs/adr-ledger/adr-ledger.edn` から統合。以後この文書は最新状態のみを表し、履歴は git が持つ。）

### 2026-07-24 — note

Implementation completed: kotoba-lang/stripe-ops built+pushed, wired into cloud-itonami as ReAct agent tools, restricted API key creation left as owner's manual step

kotoba-lang/stripe-ops repo built (governor/phase/operation/store/stripeport/advisor/sim, 21 tests / 82 assertions, clj-kondo 0 errors/warnings), pushed to GitHub, registered in west (manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects + west.yml --entry, pin verified reachable from main). Integration into orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami landed as PR #481 (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami, merge commit fa3de1dd): 3 new ReAct-agent tools (itonami_stripe_lookup / itonami_stripe_create_payment_link / itonami_stripe_confirm_payment_link) in cloud_itonami.agent, wired via cli.cljs's build-stripe-ops-actor (mock-stripeport default; live-stripeport opt-in only when STRIPE_OPS_RESTRICTED_KEY is present in env). Verified end-to-end: direct smoke test of the lookup/propose/confirm flow against mock-stripeport, backward-compat confirmed (omitting :stripe-ops-actor yields the original 3-tool list unchanged), clj-kondo clean on both edited cloud-itonami files, shadow-cljs agent-cli build compiles and the resulting CLI starts cleanly. cloud-itonami's own :test runner is currently broken for unrelated, pre-existing reasons (confirmed via git stash that the identical compile error -- engine-db/fresh-conn missing var in cloud_itonami/ops.cljc -- exists on main without this change). Outstanding: the Stripe Dashboard restricted-API-key creation itself (Customers/Subscriptions/Products/Prices read + Payment Links write only) was deliberately NOT performed by the agent (credential-form safety floor) -- this remains the owner's manual step before live-stripeport can be used; the actor runs mock-only until then.
")))
